\f1\fs20 The Jungle Room in Graceland, the iconic home of Elvis Presley located in Memphis, Tennessee, is one of the most famous and unique rooms in the estate. Decorated in the mid-1970s, the room boasts an eclectic and exotic style inspired by Polynesian and African jungle motifs, reflecting Elvis' adventurous spirit and love for the exotic.\
\
Decor:\
The walls and floor of the Jungle Room are covered in green shag carpet, creating a lush and immersive atmosphere reminiscent of a tropical rainforest floor. The ceiling is adorned with wooden beams and features a unique waterfall made from natural stone, which adds to the room's ambiance. The windows are covered with heavy, dark curtains, and the lighting is dim and moody to evoke a sense of mystery.\
\
Furniture:\
The furniture in the Jungle Room is a mix of styles, incorporating pieces that are both comfortable and visually striking. The centerpiece is a large, custom-made, round wooden table with a glass top, surrounded by matching chairs that feature animal print upholstery. A low-slung, carved wooden sofa with oversized cushions in earthy tones invites relaxation, while a tiki-style wooden bar and stools provide a spot for entertaining guests. Additional seating is provided by a rattan chair with an animal print cushion, and a throne-like chair made of wood and adorned with faux fur.\
\
Bric-a-brac:\
The Jungle Room is filled with an assortment of decorative items and curiosities that reflect its theme. Among these are carved wooden statues and masks, tribal-inspired artwork, and various animal figurines, such as elephants and monkeys. An assortment of large, leafy plants helps to enhance the jungle atmosphere, and a collection of natural artifacts, like geodes and fossils, adds an air of exploration and discovery. The room is also peppered with small touches of Elvis' personal style, including a vintage reel-to-reel tape recorder and a collection of vinyl records, which serve as reminders of the King of Rock and Roll's presence in the space.\
\
\
